und" class="lucide lucide-ellipsis size-5" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1"></circle><circle cx="19" cy="12" r="1"></circle><circle cx="5" cy="12" r="1"></circle></svg></span><span class="button-state-spinner absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-loader-circle animate-spin size-4" role="status" aria-label="Loading"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-6.219-8.56"></path></svg></span><span class="button-state-success absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check size-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span></button><a class="relative inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-3 whitespace-nowrap font-basel-medium transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:[&amp;_*]:text-inherit cursor-pointer [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-6 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 border-0 bg-accent1 text-white hover:bg-[#E500A5] disabled:bg-surface2 disabled:text-neutral3 disabled:opacity-100 rounded-12 py-2 text-button-3 h-9 px-4" href="/dashboard" data-discover="true">API keys</a></div></div></header><main class="flex-1 flex flex-col"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"Uniswap Protocols Overview","description":"Navigate the Uniswap protocol documentation, from the core AMM versions to supporting infrastructure contracts.","url":"https://developers.uniswap.org/docs/protocols/overview","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://developers.uniswap.org/docs/protocols/overview"},"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Uniswap Labs","url":"https://uniswap.org"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Uniswap","url":"https://uniswap.org","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://app.uniswap.org/favicon.png"}},"proficiencyLevel":"Beginner","audience":{"@type":"Audience","audienceType":"Developers"},"dateModified":"2026-08-27T21:02:25.000Z","keywords":"Uniswap protocols, AMM versions, Universal Router, Permit2, The Compact, protocol fees"}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Docs","item":"https://developers.uniswap.org/docs"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Protocols","item":"https://developers.uniswap.org/docs/protocols"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Uniswap Protocols Overview"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Uniswap protocol version should I use for a new integration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Uniswap v4 is the current and recommended version for new integrations. It consolidates all pools into a single PoolManager contract, supports hooks that customize pool behavior across the pool lifecycle, and uses flash accounting to defer token transfers until the end of a transaction, which reduces gas for multi-step operations. Use v3 for existing concentrated liquidity integrations and v2 for legacy constant product workflows."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between the Uniswap AMM and its supporting protocols?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The AMM contracts are the pool contracts that hold liquidity and execute swaps, versioned as Uniswap v2, v3, and v4. The supporting protocols are infrastructure contracts used across versions: the Universal Router composes swaps across v2, v3, and v4 in a single transaction, Permit2 handles signature-based token transfers and time-bound allowances, Fee Adapter and TokenJar contracts collect protocol fees, The Compact provides ERC-6909 resource locks for cross-chain coordination, and Calibur powers smart wallet delegation through EIP-7702."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which contract should I use to execute Uniswap swaps programmatically?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Universal Router is the recommended entry point for executing swaps programmatically. It is an unowned, non-upgradeable contract that composes swaps across Uniswap v2, v3, and v4 in a single transaction using command-based encoding, and it integrates with Permit2 for signature-controlled token approvals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are the Uniswap protocol contracts audited?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Uniswap v4 core and periphery repositories publish their audit reports, and Uniswap Labs maintains an active bug bounty program on Cantina for eligible vulnerability disclosures."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do I find Uniswap contract deployment addresses?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The unified deployments page at developers.uniswap.org/deployments lists Uniswap contract addresses across all protocols and chains. Each protocol section of the docs also has its own deployments page; for example, Uniswap v4 addresses are on the v4 deployments page, and the smart wallet deployments page lists the Calibur address across supported networks."}}]}</script><div id="nd-docs-layout" class="grid transition-[grid-template-columns] overflow-x-clip min-h-(--fd-docs-height) auto-cols-auto auto-rows-auto [--fd-docs-height:100dvh] [--fd-header-height:0px] [--fd-toc-popover-height:0px] [--fd-sidebar-width:0px] [--fd-toc-width:0px]" data-sidebar-collapsed="false" style="grid-template:&quot;sidebar header toc&quot;
        &quot;sidebar toc-popover toc&quot;
